# Whoosh! needs two blue for its kicker (CR 702.33a): with one blue source (Mox Sapphire among Ruby, Jet, Pearl) the kicked cast stops at its
# pay prompt, which offers nothing but Cancel, though the unkicked cast is affordable; that one returns Bot2's Ornithopter and draws nothing
# (hand 4 -> 3). Bot2's Island is a land and is not a legal target (refused); the target "nonland permanent" is anyone's.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Whoosh!
Island x2
Island x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Island x4
Island x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
! Bot1.Hand.Whoosh!.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Island)
Bot1.Hand.Whoosh!.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter; Kicked: 1)
Bot1.Cancel
Bot1.Hand.Whoosh!.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield = Island; Mox Ruby
Bot1.Hand.Count = 3
Bot1.Graveyard = Whoosh!
